WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:05.360
Mō tātou, a, mō ka uri a muri ake nei

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.820
Here we are on a nice, sunny, winter's day
on the south bank of the Kaiapoi River.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.780
The object of our endeavours was to link the
library and the main street

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.420
with the river bank.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:30.680
Lot's of boardwalk, seating, areas for children
to fish, and the whole thing is just on finished

00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:35.270
and the grass seed is down and when that grows,
the project will be finished.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:39.500
And of course the whole thing compliments
our terraces across the river in front of

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.840
Jedd's proposed new scheme.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.720
So this month is all about the waterfront
development here in Kaiapoi.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.620
As Al has already mentioned, a lot's already been completed

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.360
and it's starting to look really good.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:57.460
Next up for construction, is the boardwalk
and seating area

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:58.780
on the north bank of the river.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.960
Kevin Dwyer is the landscape architect who
has been working on the designs.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:07.799
So Kevin, can you tell us what's happening
in this part of the river?

00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:12.579
Just behind us here is going to be a private
development, hospitality and retail and fronting

00:01:12.579 --> 00:01:17.259
that is going to be a boardwalk that links
the town centre across the front of the new

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:20.140
development and down towards the riverbank
walkway.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:25.780
Fronting the timber boardwalk is a series
of concrete terraces with built-in timber

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.429
seating that leads down to the top of the
riverbank, and that will be a really nice

00:01:29.429 --> 00:01:32.600
space for people to come down, have their
lunch, have a cup of coffee

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.040
and interact more with the river.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.640
And what are some of the challenges that you
are facing with this project?

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:42.400
We've had to integrate our design with the design
of the private development and also

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.180
the rebuild of the stopbank wall by ECAN.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:49.180
And it's just the timing of that, and getting
the design, working together

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.000
It's probably been the biggest challenge so far.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:57.700
Construction should begin later this year,
and is expected to be completed in 2018.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:02.560
Work also continues with local developer,
Jedd Pearce on a proposed riverfront

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.360
shopping and dining complex.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:09.800
Preliminary designs are complete, with a microbrewery
and bar proposed as an anchor tenant.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:13.180
The design of the building will allow visitors
to experience the brewing process,

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.560
while enjoying food and views of the river.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:22.100
As part of the riverfront enhancement, we’ve
placed a new information panel opposite the library.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:26.560
This is one more way that the local community
can keep up to date with the latest developments.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:32.030
Currently we seeking feedback on two roading
options for access to the new sport and recreation

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:34.700
reserve in the Kaiapoi East Regeneration Area.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:41.240
In Option 1, Cass Street remains open to access
the reserve, rural area and private property.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.260
Option 2, is an alternative where Cass Street
is closed to vehicles at the entrance to the

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.780
reserve and Jollie Street is reinstated.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:51.600
We’d love to hear what option you prefer.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:58.380
Next update, we’ll be meeting some Kaiapoi
students who have big ideas for the Regeneration

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.360
and looking at the ways local youth can have
their say.

